    bd_faq_title:'FAQ — Bangladeshi Workers in Oman',
    bd_faq1_q:'Do Bangladeshi expats in Oman pay SPF deductions?', bd_faq1_a:'No. The Social Protection Fund (SPF) 8% deduction applies only to Omani nationals. Bangladeshi and other expatriate workers keep their full gross salary with no SPF deduction.',
    bd_faq2_q:'How is end-of-service gratuity calculated for Bangladeshis in Oman?', bd_faq2_a_html:'Under Article 61 of Oman Labour Law: 1 month basic salary per year of service, with partial years pro-rated. Example: 5 years at OMR 350 basic salary = OMR 1,750 gratuity. Use the <a href="end-of-service.html" style="color:var(--primary);">End of Service Calculator</a> for your exact figure.',
    bd_faq3_q:'Is there income tax on salary in Oman for Bangladeshi workers?', bd_faq3_a:'As of 2026, Oman does not impose personal income tax on salaries. A Personal Income Tax law was enacted in 2025 but is scheduled to take effect from 2028. Currently no tax deduction applies to Bangladeshi workers\' salaries in Oman.',
    bd_faq4_q:'What is the best way to send money from Oman to Bangladesh?', bd_faq4_a_html:'Popular services include: bank wire transfers, exchange houses (Al Ansari, Western Union), and online platforms (bKash-compatible services, Wise, Remitly). Compare rates before sending. Use the <a href="currency-converter.html" style="color:var(--primary);">OMR to BDT Currency Converter</a> to check the live rate.',
    bd_faq5_q:'What labour rights do Bangladeshi workers have in Oman?', bd_faq5_a:'Oman Labour Law protects all workers regardless of nationality. Key rights: end-of-service gratuity (Article 61), 1 month notice period, 30 days annual leave after 1 year of service, and the right to file a complaint at the Ministry of Labour if your employer violates your contract.',
